## Running

```sh
{% if port and entrypoint != 'none' -%}
docker run --rm -p {{ port }}:{{ port }} {{ image }}
{%- elif entrypoint == 'entrypoint' -%}
docker run --rm {{ image }} --help
{%- elif entrypoint == 'cmd' -%}
docker run --rm {{ image }} {{ project_name }} --help
{%- else -%}
docker run --rm {{ image }} <script> --help
{%- endif %}
```

{% if entrypoint == 'none' -%}
The image has no entry point: name one of the console scripts in
`pyproject.toml`'s `[project.scripts]`. {% endif -%}
The image runs as uid {{ image_uid }} and works with a read-only root filesystem;
mount a writable `/tmp`{% if writable_dirs.split() %} and {% for d in writable_dirs.split() %}`{{ d }}`{{ ', ' if not loop.last else '' }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.

## Versions

{% if ships_releases -%}
Releases are the git tags `vX.Y.Z`. A weekly CI run (Monday 06:00 UTC)
tags the next version when a `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `revert` or breaking
commit landed, or a maintenance patch when dependency updates are waiting;
a CVE fix releases on the push that brings it. Only a tag builds and pushes
the image, as `X.Y.Z`, `X.Y` and `latest`, with the version in its
`org.opencontainers.image.version` label. `version` in `pyproject.toml` is a
placeholder and stays `0.0.0`.
{%- else -%}
There are no releases. Every push to main that changes the image publishes
it as `sha-<commit>`{% if cloud_run != 'none' %} and deploys it to the Cloud Run {{ cloud_run }}{% endif %}.
`version` in `pyproject.toml` is a placeholder and stays `0.0.0`.
{%- endif %}

## Development

```sh
uv run pytest                     # with the coverage gate from pyproject.toml
uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format --check .
pre-commit install                # the same checks before each commit
docker build -t {{ project_name }} .
```

Dependencies resolve only to releases at least 7 days old (`exclude-newer`
in `pyproject.toml`), and the image installs exactly what `uv.lock` pins.
To take a CVE fix released less than 7 days ago, add the package to
`exclude-newer-package` as `<name> = false`, run `uv lock`, and remove the
entry once the release is a week old.

The skeleton (Dockerfile, CI, lint and test configuration) comes from
[python-app-template](https://github.com/mbologna/python-app-template);
Renovate proposes its updates as pull requests.
